  "worked_solution": "We compute the dot product between $u$ and each of the listed vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot (-3)+4\\cdot (-1)+3\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =2+3-4-3 \\\\  & =-2.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot w & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {w}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {w}_{4} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 5+(-1)\\cdot 0+4\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =5-8+3 \\\\  & =0.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot x & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {x}_{4} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot (-2)+4\\cdot 3+3\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =1+2+12-15 \\\\  & =0.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the correct option is $w$ and $x$ only.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
